<title>NETHERLANDS: Fortis sees profit up 10-15 pct.</title>
<headline>Fortis sees profit up 10-15 pct.</headline>
<dateline>UTRECHT, Netherlands 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch-Belgian financial group Fortis said on Wednesday it expected full-year net profit for 1997 to show a rise of 10 to 15 percent compared with 1996.  </p>
<p>Fortis said its two parent companies, Fortis Amev and Fortis AG, both expected full-year 1997 earnings per share to show a rise of 10 to 15 percent compared with 1996.  </p>
<p>Dutch parent Fortis Amev earlier reported a net profit of 224 million guilders for the first quarter of 1997, up from 171 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>Belgian parent Fortis AG announced a first quarter net profit of 3.97 billion Belgian francs, versus 2.73 billion in the first quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
